<Wiki
  title="puv php"
  description="List, install, and remove StaticPHP CLI runtimes for Linux glibc."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>php</h1>
  <p>
    <code>puv php</code> manages runtimes on the machine. The project pin is
    <a href="/wiki/commands/use"><code>puv use</code></a>. These commands install and remove
    builds without being that pin. Runtimes are prebuilt StaticPHP CLI builds for Linux glibc,
    <code>x86_64</code> and <code>aarch64</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>List</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv php list
puv php list --all</pre>
  <p>
    <code>puv php list</code> shows installed runtimes.
    <code>puv php list --all</code> shows installed and not-yet-installed releases.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv php install 8.3
puv php install 8.3.32
puv php install --all</pre>
  <ul>
    <li><code>8.3</code> installs every 8.3 patch.</li>
    <li><code>8.3.32</code> installs that patch only.</li>
    <li><code>--all</code> installs the whole index.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A download prints a progress line on stderr. A cached archive stays quiet. Installed builds
    live under <code>~/.local/share/puv/</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Installing 8.3 this way does not change <code>php</code> in <code>puv.toml</code>.
    <code>puv use 8.3</code> does, and it records the exact patch.
  </p>

  <h2>Remove</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv php remove 8.3
puv php remove --all</pre>
  <ul>
    <li><code>8.3</code> removes every installed 8.3 patch.</li>
    <li><code>--all</code> removes every runtime puv installed.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Cache archives can remain after the install is gone.
    <a href="/wiki/commands/prune"><code>puv prune --global</code></a> drops cache entries nothing
    references.
  </p>
</Wiki>
